CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ rewritten < from <=>: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ other rewritten comparisons: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ noexcept of rewritten \(not noexcept here\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
static assertion failed
dropped the body
--
N5008 [over.match.oper]/3.4: for `x @ y' with @ relational the candidate
set includes the rewritten `(x <=> y) @ 0' and reversed `0 @ (y <=> x)';
for `!=' the rewritten `!(x == y)'; the operator<=> / operator== may be a
friend or namespace-scope function.  Previously only a MEMBER operator<=>
was tried and the synthesized comparison against 0 was left un-type-checked
("warning: ignoring <"), so std::three_way_comparable_with (whose
requires-expression tests `__t < __u') was false for every class with a
defaulted or friend <=>.  [expr.unary.noexcept]/3: the operand is
potentially-throwing if any call in it, at any depth, is -- `noexcept(p <
q)' rewritten to `(p <=> q) < 0' must see the potentially-throwing <=>
under the category's noexcept operator<.
